  "summary": "I wrote the coin dash game in `src/main.ts`. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so it hasn't been run or seen rendering.\n\n- **Scene and gameplay:** A sphere player moves on a flat arena with arrow keys or WASD. There are 10 coins. Touching one gives +1 score and respawns it elsewhere, using a seeded random generator so runs repeat. The scene is drawn with Aura3D (`createAuraApp`, the `neon-arcade` look, primitives).\n- **Timestep:** The simulation advances in fixed 1/60 s steps from an accumulator in a `requestAnimationFrame` loop. Time is counted in whole frames, so 30.0 s is exactly 1800 steps.\n- **Round rules:** Reaching 15 coins sets `won` immediately. Reaching 30 s with fewer sets `lost`. `P` toggles pause, which freezes the simulation. `R` resets score, timer, coin layout and status.\n- **HUD and hooks:** A DOM HUD below the canvas has elements with ids `score`, `time` and `status`. `window.__EVAL__ = { state, step }` is exposed. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set once the first frame has been presented.\n\nOne choice the task left open: `step(n)` does nothing while the game is paused, won or lost. It uses whatever movement keys are held at the time.\n\n",
